
🛰️ Spacecraft Constellation Fault Simulator

A GUI-based spacecraft constellation simulator built on the Basilisk framework. It allows simulation of multiple satellites, injection of realistic reaction wheel faults, and analysis of fault effects using plots and 3D visualisation through Vizard.

Overview
This simulator is designed for:
•	Modeling and managing multi-satellite constellations
•	Injecting faults like encoder drift, friction increase, power limits, and battery degradation
•	Visualizing scenarios in Unity-based Vizard
•	Logging telemetry and creating .bin files for later playback
•	Exporting data for performance evaluation and debugging
 Features
•	Multi-satellite support with up to 20 satellites
•	Four realistic fault types with configurable parameters
•	Ground target assignment and camera targeting
•	GUI for fault configuration, simulation control, and output analysis
•	Vizard-compatible .bin generation
•	Plotting and telemetry logging



