Quick Start

cd core
python run_fault_simulator.py

GUI Guide
Tabs Overview:
1.	Constellation Tab – Configure satellites, orbits, and quick-setup presets.
2.	Fault Tab – Select fault type, magnitude, timing, and assign it to a satellite.
3.	Targets Tab – Assign observation targets to each satellite.
4.	Visualization Tab – Set camera views and visualization settings for Vizard.
5.	Output Tab – Choose run duration, log options, and enable .bin generation.
6.	Results Tab – View and export plots of satellite behavior and fault impact.

Simulation Workflow
1.	Select Constellation → default setup or custom.
2.	Add Faults → encoder, power limit, etc.
3.	Assign Targets → random or manual lat/lon input.
4.	Run Simulation → generate .bin file and logs.
5.	Visualise in Vizard → load .bin for analysis.

Fault Types
Fault Type	Description	Effect
Friction Fault	Simulates rotor resistance	Reduced agility
Power Limit Fault	Limits motor power	Delayed maneuvers
Encoder Fault	Introduces sensor error	Inaccurate attitude control
Battery Fault	Adds power drain	Reduced runtime

📂 Output Files

•	Logs: logs/sim_results_*/
•	Plots: plots/
•	Vizard: Vizfile/_VizFiles/*.bin

Troubleshooting


Issue	Fix
Vizard not showing satellite	Make sure .bin file is generated
Camera not aiming at target	Validate pointing vector config
GUI not opening	Check tkinter is installed
Module errors	Ensure Basilisk is in Python PATH

